# Echo campaign B, re-run of one test: nosleep (10,000 clients at once, 5 rounds) in Docker only.
# In echo-new (results/2026-10-16_200724) this test lost ~20% of its connections ("connection reset") for every
# server, C included, and none natively: Docker's port relay uses two ports per connection, a closed connection
# keeps its port for 60 s (TIME_WAIT), and the ~28,000 ports ran out from round 3 (reproduced by hand 2026-10-17).
# ENV_TCP_TW_REUSE=1 lets Linux reuse those ports early (by hand: 0 failures in all 5 rounds); restored after.
# Same settings as echo-new otherwise. 4 servers x 5 repeats = 20 measurements, about 30 min.
#   make run CONFIG=campaigns/paper/echo-new-docker-nosleep.config
MACHINE=minimal
ENV_CPU_SPEED=1800
ENV_TCP_TW_REUSE=1
MEASURE=echo
VARIANTS=nobw:ERL_FLAGS=+sbwt none +sbwtdcpu none +sbwtdio none
DEPLOY=container
REPEATS=5
IDLE_SECONDS=0
ECHO_CONNECT_CLIENTS=
ECHO_NOSLEEP_CLIENTS=10000
ECHO_NOSLEEP_ROUNDS=5
ECHO_BURST_CLIENTS=
ECHO_STREAM_CLIENTS=
ECHO_SIZES_BYTES=15
